Number = {3},
Pages = {655-673},
Month = {SEP},
Abstract = {How does the enterprise of political theory create and sustain the
   borders that account for its appearance as a distinguishable profession?
   In this article, the author considers and criticizes a recent effort to
   defend political theory's right to exist in the form of one of several
   subfields constitutive of the academic discipline of professional
   political science in the United States. The author closes by suggesting
   that theorists might be better positioned to think critically about
   politics, and the politics of liberalism more particularly, if this
   self-representation were to be unsettled and possibly jettisoned
   altogether.},
