   simultaneous appeals to the diversity of human practices and eternal
   norms of Justice Isaiah Berlin famously referred to tins as an
   impassable ``contradiction{''} burdening Ins work Careful examination of
   Rousseau's appropriations from and developments on Montesquieu, however,
   reveal that these observations are not merely reconcilable-they provide
   a fruitful way to approach legislation and constitution drafting This is
   accomplished by understanding his employment of the principle of
